From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jfacemyer <1776340+jfacemyer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 07:30:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dwrite: Key cached glyph bitmaps by rendering mode.

The glyph cache keyed rendered bitmaps by glyph and size only, under the
same key as the natural-mode advance and bbox entries. An aliased bitmap
is 1 bit per pixel and the other modes 8, so a glyph rendered
antialiased and later aliased (or the other way round) had its cached
bitmap memcpy'd into a buffer sized for the other mode: a heap overflow
that corrupted unrelated memory and crashed later. Upstream Wine has the
same code.

The rendering mode is now part of a bitmap's key, and a cached bitmap
whose size differs from the requested one is not copied; the glyph is
rendered directly instead.

Adapted from neutron-wine (Nico-LaFoucate), whose fix is written against
their transform-keyed cache; only the mode key and the size check are
taken.
---
 dlls/dwrite/font.c | 14 +++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/dwrite/font.c b/dlls/dwrite/font.c
index 5d4f156..74d3309 100644
--- a/dlls/dwrite/font.c
+++ b/dlls/dwrite/font.c
@@ -196,7 +196,9 @@ static unsigned int get_glyph_bitmap_pitch(DWRITE_RENDERING_MODE1 rendering_mode
 static HRESULT dwrite_fontface_get_glyph_bitmap(struct dwrite_fontface *fontface, DWRITE_RENDERING_MODE1 rendering_mode,
         unsigned int *is_1bpp, struct dwrite_glyphbitmap *bitmap)
 {
-    struct cache_key key = { .size = bitmap->emsize, .glyph = bitmap->glyph, .mode = DWRITE_MEASURING_MODE_NATURAL };
+    /* Aliased bitmaps are 1 bpp and the others 8 bpp, so bitmaps are keyed by rendering mode,
+       kept apart from the advance and bbox entries keyed by measuring mode. */
+    struct cache_key key = { .size = bitmap->emsize, .glyph = bitmap->glyph, .mode = 0x100 | rendering_mode };
     struct get_glyph_bitmap_params params;
     const RECT *bbox = &bitmap->bbox;
     unsigned int bitmap_size, _1bpp;
@@ -225,9 +227,15 @@ static HRESULT dwrite_fontface_get_glyph_bitmap(struct dwrite_fontface *fontface
     }
     else if ((entry = fontface_get_cache_entry(fontface, bitmap_size, &key)))
     {
-        if (entry->has_bitmap)
+        if (entry->has_bitmap && entry->bitmap_size == bitmap_size)
         {
             memcpy(bitmap->buf, entry->bitmap, entry->bitmap_size);
+            *is_1bpp = entry->is_1bpp;
+        }
+        else if (entry->has_bitmap)
+        {
+            /* Never copy a cached bitmap into a buffer sized for another one. */
+            UNIX_CALL(get_glyph_bitmap, &params);
         }
         else
         {
@@ -239,8 +247,8 @@ static HRESULT dwrite_fontface_get_glyph_bitmap(struct dwrite_fontface *fontface
                 memcpy(entry->bitmap, bitmap->buf, entry->bitmap_size);
             entry->is_1bpp = !!_1bpp;
             entry->has_bitmap = 1;
+            *is_1bpp = entry->is_1bpp;
         }
-        *is_1bpp = entry->is_1bpp;
     }
     else
         hr = E_FAIL;
